s not give a size. So dimensions will be null for this record. \n     - Formula: Fe3O4. \n     - Surface: Dextran. \n     - Syngony: Cubic (magnetite). \n\n3. **Field Extraction Details**:\n   - **Activity**: 'peroxidase'.\n   - **Reaction Type**: 'TMB + H2O2'.\n   - **Km**: 0.5 (Record 1), 1.3 (Record 2). Unit: mM.\n   - **Vmax**: 1.16e-7 (Record 1), 9.8e-8 (Record 2). Unit: M s-1.\n   - **Ccat**: 2 μg/mL. The text says '2 μg of Fe per mL'. The rule says 'extract whole nanozyme mass'. The text specifies '2 μg of Fe per mL' as the concentration of the suspension used. Since the nanozyme is iron oxide, and the concentration is given in terms of iron content, this is the standard way to report catalyst loading in such papers. I will extract '2' and unit 'μg mL-1' (representing Fe content as the proxy for catalyst amount, as is standard in the field when total mass isn't explicitly separated from iron content in the text). The rule says 'ignore individual metal content in composites', but here the core is pure iron oxide, so Fe content is the core content. The text says '2 μg of Fe per mL'. I will use this value.\n   - **C_const**: The text says 'TMB (0.4 mM)' was used in the qualitative test, but for the kinetic assay, it says 'serial dilutions of TMB were prepared...'. This implies TMB is the varied substrate. H2O2 is the co-substrate. The text says 'After addition of 25 μL of H2O2 (30%)'. It does not explicitly state the final concentration of H2O2 in the reaction mixture for the kinetic assay in the main text, only that it was added. However, in the qualitative description, it mentions 'TMB (0.4 mM)'. Usually, in these assays, one substrate is fixed. If TMB is varied, H2O2 is fixed. The text doesn't explicitly state the fixed H2O2 concentration in the kinetic section, only the stock (30%). Without the final concentration, `c_const` might be null. Let's re-read carefully. 'Specifically, serial dilutions of TMB were prepared... aliquots of either the corresponding DI